proof.text:
For the identity supports, $\mu$ and the exceptional adjunction in [def-trf-supported-pairing] are unit identifications, so the pairing is its contraction of $\widetilde u\otimes\widetilde v$. A summand has factor order $U(e_{i,a}),\epsilon_{i,a},\phi_{j,b},V(f_{j,b})$. To apply $\operatorname{ev}_T\otimes\operatorname{ev}_B$, move $\phi_{j,b}$ past $\epsilon_{i,a}$ and $U(e_{i,a})$, leaving order $\phi_{j,b},U(e_{i,a}),\epsilon_{i,a},V(f_{j,b})$. The additional Koszul sign is $(-1)^{(-j)(-i+i)}=1$. Evaluation is zero unless $i=j$, and the finite dual-frame identity for $T^i$ gives
$$
\begin{aligned}
\langle u,v\rangle_{\mathrm{LV}}
&=\sum_{i,a,b}(-1)^i\phi_{i,b}(U(e_{i,a}))\epsilon_{i,a}(V(f_{i,b}))\\
&=\sum_{i,a}(-1)^i\epsilon_{i,a}(VU(e_{i,a})).
\end{aligned}
$$
Apply the defining trace composite of [def-trf-categorical-trace] to $VU$ on $B$: coevaluation sends $1$ to $\sum_{i,a}e_{i,a}\otimes\epsilon_{i,a}$; $VU\otimes1$ sends it to $\sum_{i,a}VU(e_{i,a})\otimes\epsilon_{i,a}$; symmetry contributes $(-1)^{i(-i)}=(-1)^i$; evaluation gives the last displayed sum. Thus the pairing equals $\operatorname{tr}_A(vu\mid P)$. This is equality of the specified derived morphisms by the model comparison in Step 1; conjugating the representative of $vu$ leaves its trace unchanged by [prop-trf-trace-formal-laws] (conjugacy invariance). The calculation uses finite dual frames and allows nonzero differentials.
